  "content_description": "",
  "content_text_body": "Recognizing, accepting, and implementing creative ideas from team members communicates to the whole team that changes are the norm. The objective here is to create a culture where ingenuity is valued so that processes that support change are already in place. \n\n### Avoid thinking in terms of best versus worst\nRather than searching for all the flaws in an idea, focus on its potential benefits. Ask yourself:\n* What would be the ROI of making this change? \n* Do the potential benefits outweigh the potential costs?\n* What excites you about the idea?\n\nWhen in doubt, ask your team to evaluate new ideas. Be sure to evaluate how good the potential benefits would be and how bad the potential risks could be. If the risks are minimal, implementing a new idea has the additional benefit of helping the team overcome fear of change.",
